00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
hello and welcome to the new old review  your source for everything anime manga  and today we are back with some more  black clover review style things or i  guess things singular because it's just  one but this just one thing happens to  be the hot springs training camp arc the  shortest since our initial outings in  the series but a great experience with a  ton of character development and  in-world  intrigue to be had it's definitely not  quite what i was expecting when i first  heard the name of the arc but as always  if you are enjoying these videos then  please do activate your finger motion  and direct it towards both the like and  subscribe buttons because i can't  really read comments due to spoilers but  i can see numbers so if you want more of  this  allegedly black clover then don't forget  to do the thing but starting with the  premise of the arc it starts out almost  exactly the same as the eye of the  midnight sun arc with aster being  ordered to take some time off except  this time instead of becoming embroiled  in an epic clash against wildly powerful  magic smiths we actually do take the  time to breathe and go to a festival  followed by a brief burst of training  and on paper that's kind of that  and as sort of mundane as it sounds i  really appreciated it and i think it  worked quite well  firstly because it breaks the now  established black clover pattern we got  through a handful of medium-sized darks  that all had very similar constructive  tissue you know we get a call to action  explore a new location face off against  an enemy far greater than anyone was  prepared for defeat them anyway and then  move on to do it all again which isn't  to say that's a bad thing because tabata  tweaks that formula just enough to keep  things interesting but this 10 chapter  arc is very much what i was looking for  right about now and it made me aware of  something very intriguing actually which  is that the characters of this series  are just so strong that we don't  actually need a conflict or big bad  enemies to make black clover captivating  because i really was more than happy  just following all of our protagonistic  misfits and watching them interact with  each other for this block of time and in  many ways it was almost like reading a  more light-hearted high school comedy  series so that was a cool change of pace  and it was great to take some time to  breathe and have fun after this string  of massive action pieces but our first  point to focus here was the star  festival an annual event where we get to  find out which of the magic knight  squads impressed senpai the most and  earned the greatest amount of delicious  star merits and there was some very  expected stuff here for example the  golden dawn obviously won and yuno was  obviously recognized for his absurdly  great rookie efforts what i did not  expect was for the black bulls to rank  smack bang in second place when the  ceremony began i thought to myself that  they'd either still be last but with a  positive amount of stars or that they  would beat a single squad and still be  just as shocked as they ultimately were  to come second  screw that though we're jumping straight  into second place which seems a bit  sudden but at the same time i believe  the wizard king said that astor was now  16 as of the time of this festival which  i think means that a whole year has  already passed since we received the  grimoire and joined the black bulls  which is kind of wild because my  perception of time was something like i  don't know a few months but i do like it  one of my personal annoyances when it  comes to shona manga is not having that  passage of time or a super slow passage  like a my hero academia sort of feel  where after almost 300 chapters deku is  still in his first year of high school  or food wars where the vast majority of  it also takes place in soma's first year  but then again i have to say i'm also a  pretty massive hypocrite because i love  one piece and the first  almost 600 chapters of that basically  play out over the course of a few months  so  yeah in conclusion i like that astor is  older and that time is progressing at a  nice pace and me being me i also really  enjoyed seeing the list of all the  reasons why the stars were awarded this  is the kind of little detail that  tabitha really did not need to include  he could have just thrown a total amount  up there and it would have been just as  effective but i like that he took the  time to work out in great detail where  the golden dawn specifically earned all  of their stars and of course this arc  actually marks a major step forward for  the astor yuna rivalry because both of  them get recognized on stage by mr  wizard king  and they well they decide to show off a  bit in order to win the favor or at  least respect of the crowd and this is a  much bigger moment than any kind of  power  up or increase in rank because here you  have the wizard king very publicly  raising their profiles  and practically holding them up as the  base standard of the magic knight system  so we're starting to break through the  discrimination aspect of them being  lowly peasantry or at least with the  general crowd anyway although to be fair  the crowd here are just kind of upper  class plebs themselves  most of them aren't high high nobility  so i'm sure there's still an extremely  prevalent faction of noble supremacy  which sure speaking of we get to meet  the uh the actual king during this arc  a very very disappointing man by the  name of augustus kira clover viii  who spends most of his time here  commanding to be glorified simply due to  the achievement of existing and all i  can really say is that he looks acts and  sounds exactly like i was expecting  especially the looks he's such a  standard royal  king dude bro almost like he was pulled  straight out of a box of a children's  court playset so i actually find him  quite boring as a result i think that  tabitha could have gone to some more  extremes with his design you know make  him a lot uglier or even a lot prettier  just something to make him actually  stand out  unless of course that's the whole point  a purposely boring and underwhelming  figurehead of nobility  i don't know even then i just i don't  care for him like it's not even that i  don't like him i just don't  care at all for the king currently it's  very neutral however the king did have  something interesting to say though  which i imagine seeds a future rock  which is that he plans to build a force  of royal knights and have them directly  attack the eye of the midnight sun which  brings up questions ever so many  questions some of which posed directly  by astor  for example why should we be under your  command for such an important task when  we have a much more capable military  leader in the wizard king and also at  least one from me being  what is even the point of going through  this test surely if you wanted to do  something like this you just  instruct the majority of the magic  knights to do so because they're already  kind of under your command as king and  if you did indeed want some kind of  super squad then just scoop up all of  the captains maybe the vice captains  and form it that way so beyond being a  [ __ ] i really don't quite get the  purpose of what the king is doing here  at the moment but i'm sure his  motivations will become clearer in the  future or not i'm actually not sure of  that so i shouldn't say that but i did  and re-recording it would be a mild  inconvenience so  i'm not going to redo it but something  else i wanted to highlight from the star  festival though is the appearance of  kyoto and kohono  it was nice to see them again and have  them healed by the blood magic of the  witch queen  but it was also kind of annoying because  the whole thing with the underwater  temple was that they had dreams of  traveling to the surface  and being performers but were unable to  do so for unspecified reasons  they just you know weren't allowed to go  to the capitol because it was  and i quote against the rules but here  they both are  in the capital and it's one of those  things where it could have been fixed  with just one line saying something like  our grandfather gave us permission to  travel to the capital for this one day  or just  something anything i'm still kind of  annoyed that we never really got to  explore the culture of the sea folk or  find out why they were so purposely  self-isolated but after the whole star  festival business things get very  suddenly amazing with the introduction  of a certain maria leona vermillion who  from here on out i will only refer to as  cisco leon because it's much easier to  say  and it's kind of adorable but i really  do love this whole family the vermillion  family and the crimson lions are easily  one of my favorite factions in the  series and cisco leon does not  disappoint at all i love her fiery  nature i thought it was hilarious that  she managed to conscript everyone  including two magic knight captains into  her scheme and i really do like that she  managed to continue the whole fuegoleon  legacy of inspiration i mean cisco leon  is certainly much more  brutal than fuego leon but she managed  to push both astor and noel in exactly  the right direction very much mirroring  the actions of her brother except i  suppose actually fuego leon influenced  both aster and noewell with profound  words meanwhile cisco leon did the same  but mostly through action which was a  nice contrast and in fact noelle herself  took quite a few steps forward in this  very short 10 chapters both with the  aforementioned growth with cisgolian but  also coming to her own philosophical  view on nobility and i find it a very  interesting thing that noel has chosen  to embrace her noble heritage because  usually in this sort of story the  other good noble characters would  generally come to abandon that side of  them you know the whole idea of we're  all equal so i shall cast aside  my nobility and such but here in noel's  case she chooses to recognize that  everyone is not indeed equal  she has been granted a greater level of  power than most and so she now sees it  as her having a great responsibility to  use that power to help those without it  so it's a very nice spin on the royal  character trope and after noel said that  i had the exact same reaction as aster  where i was like huh  i guess i do like noel quite a bit and  there was some more information dropped  about noel's mother the steel warrior  princess which basically represents the  polar opposite of what noel is with her  magic said to be dignified beyond all  belief  and i want to know more about her a lot  more about her because she seems like  quite a legendary figure of pure  awesomeness  and weirdly enough the more i learn  about noelle's mother the easier it  may become to empathize with noah's  siblings who to be clear are still  complete and utter bricks but there is  definitely a harsh reckoning to come to  terms with when it involves not only the  sacrifice of your mother but one of the  kingdom's greatest mages and i don't  know if black clover is the kind of  series that would go that deep but i can  see where the really twisted psyche  kicks in there and it also does put  tremendous pressure on noel to live up  to her mother's legacy a task which she  seems to have embraced and i do look  forward to seeing her progress further  and as for aster i think it's also  important to note that he seems to have  discovered a mechanism to activate his  uh well i suppose i don't  really know what to call it yet a  partial transformation leopold calls it  black aster which sure  that's fine i do like how key was worked  into it which is still  a little bit of a weird subsystem to me  but yeah whatever let's go with it and  someone else who got expanded upon quite  a bit would be the captain of the blue  rose charlotte and at the very least as  a result i can  kind of get on board with her yummy  obsession now charlotte and vanessa  actually have  shockingly similar yummy backstories  where he just stumbles in and saves them  from whatever hell they're trapped in  before casually wandering back out i do  wish that charlotte was treated a bit  more like a captain though and less like  comic relief although i do have to admit  that there was this great panel at the  end of the arc where she  was all flustered at the thought of yami  being gasped naked but i do wish that  the army obsession wasn't currently her  defining characteristic i mean for  example i really don't like noel's  sunday obsession with asta but at the  very least that part of her is always  secondary to noelle's primary  story focus which is learning to control  her power and living up to her family's  legacy but with charlotte everything is  very much geared towards yami because  her curse is directly tied to him having  stolen her heart  and yeah i don't know right now i just  find her much less interesting than most  other  characters in the series but when  everything is said and done which is  about now this was a great little minion  i applaud tamita for taking the time to  just sit and dwell on some interactions  between our main caster protagonists  whilst also finding a way to incorporate  a hell of a lot of development into it  not just emotional either because  everyone present at the training camp  got a lot of power development as well  and we got to do all of it without a  single battle required so it was a  pleasant break and some much needed  variety for the series and as a result i  feel rested rejuvenated and more than  ready to tackle our next challenge but  that pretty much does it for this blind  review of the hot springs training camp  arc and what do you guys think please do  leave your thoughts in the comments  below or even join my discord server and  if you are keen for some more black  clover content then please do go and  check out some of my other videos or  even subscribe to the channel for very  maybe regular black clover goodness  delivered straight into your youtube  feed but for now this has been the new  world review and i'll see you next time

